// Four items the collection's own "Playbill" and "Sheet Music" format filters miss: two concert
// programs and two publications, filed under "Programs/Events" and "Publication." One of them is
// the single most important item here: the complete scholarly edition of In Dahomey.
const beyond = [
  {
    title: 'The Music and Scripts of In Dahomey',
    credits: 'Edited by Thomas L. Riis',
    notes: 'Music of the United States of America, vol. 5 / Recent Researches in American Music, vol. 25. Published for the American Musicological Society by A-R Editions, 1996. 317 pages: the complete script, every musical number in full score, and a scholarly essay on the show’s genesis, creators, and performance history. Confirms Abbie Mitchell sang “Brown-Skin Baby Mine” in the original 1903 production. No playbill or sheet music for In Dahomey survives elsewhere in this collection — this book is what stands in for it.',
    href: 'https://dl.thehistorymakers.org/catalog/651805452bcbe363f26f9fbfe41042aa',
    image: imgInDahomey,
  },
  {
    title: 'Abbie Mitchell, soprano — recital program',
